    "note": "**P1 checkpoint — static composition** of `@m0saic/hero/search-typing/v1` (defaults, 1280×400, 4s still-video).\n\nWhat is composed: rounded white card + muted chrome (polygon magnifier ring, \"Search for\" label, label underline segment) + the FIRST word (\"Ideas\") fully typed in ink. **Nothing animates yet** — P2 adds the typing curtain, growing underline, and per-word windows.\n\nGeometry at this canvas: bar 794×200 centered, radius 16, icon square 84px, fontSize ~57.8px (shrink-to-fit with 8% CLI/app slack).",
    "question": "Judging ONLY the static look:\n\n1. **Ring** — does the magnifier read as a crisp ring (not a disc / square), with sane stroke weight + handle angle?\n2. **Proportions** — card size on canvas, icon/label/word scale, corner radius?\n3. **Colors** — page #F2F3F5 / card white / muted #9AA0A6 / ink #202124 feel right vs the reference?\n\nAnything off, say which of the three and I fork the fix as candidate-002.",
    "response": {
      "body": "ring looks fine. proportions seem fine too. as well as colors. approved to keep iterating",
