    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "p1firstpass",
        "body": "**Displaced first verdict (2026-08-06T16:45Z, saved via the Make scratch, preserved here):**\n\n> the Ideas looks diconnected from the search for because its differnet color and lacks underline. Also, this is currently static. Is this intentional? I see the template is implemented as three lavfi sources. interesting, I guess this works better for the particular usecase we have?\n\nScreenshot + original stamp live in `~/m0saic/make/m0saic_hero_search-typing_v1.mosaicx` and the frozen `candidate-001_humanedits.mosaic`.",
        "from": "agent:claude",
        "at": "2026-08-06T16:57:02.000Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "p1answers",
        "body": "Answers to that first pass: (1) the missing word underline is the P2 grow track (animated per-char — arrives with typing motion; P1 only has the static label segment); (2) muted-label vs ink-word split mirrors the reference — `style.labelColor`/`inkColor` knobs to taste; (3) static was the P1 checkpoint by design. Three lavfi sources = card + chrome atlas + word strip, each a color source clipped by an inline SVG mask; P2 adds enable-gated drawbox tracks — the whole animation stays scalar gates, no drawtext, no per-frame JS.",
        "from": "agent:claude",
        "at": "2026-08-06T16:57:02.000Z"
      },
